{"rule": "Return this JSON object with the rule field unchanged and a new passage of about 250 words in the text field.", "text": "By August the row had grown taller than the girl herself, and the heads turned each morning to follow the sun over the chimneys. Neighbours slowed on their way to the bus to look, and an old man from the end of the street stopped one evening to say he had not seen the like since before the war. The girl did not know which war he meant and did not ask. She only nodded and went on filling the watering can at the rain butt, carrying it slopping down the path with both hands. The crooked one at the end had caught up a little but never quite straightened, and it bloomed last of all, a small bright face no wider than a saucer, still leaning toward the fence. Her mother came out to see it in her slippers, a tea towel over one shoulder, and stood a long time with her arms folded. Then she said, quite suddenly, that her own mother had always saved the seeds from the smallest flower, because the smallest one had worked hardest to be there. The girl had not heard this before. In September she cut the heads and hung them in the shed to dry, and when they were ready she rubbed the seeds loose into a jam jar with her thumbs. She kept back twenty from the little crooked flower and folded them into an envelope. On the front, in her careful best handwriting, she wrote her cousin's address in the north, and underneath, smaller, she added: plant these first."}
